<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Node tRPC layer → Python sidecar | JSON IPC over stdin/stdout; Python receives untrusted file_path string from upload route |
| Python sidecar → filesystem | Sidecar opens user-provided file_path with `open()` |
| .docx file → ZIP/XML parser | Untrusted user-uploaded ZIP archive parsed by Python's zipfile + regex |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-16-05 | Denial of Service | zipfile.ZipFile parsing untrusted .docx | mitigate | Upload route in Plan 03 enforces 10 MB size cap before sidecar is invoked; zipfile reads fully into BytesIO so a >10MB compressed bomb cannot reach this code path |
| T-16-06 | Tampering | file_path parameter from Node → Python | mitigate | Path validation done at upload route (Plan 03) which only allows files under `./uploads/templates/`; sidecar trusts the validated path |
| T-16-07 | Information Disclosure | Error messages may leak filesystem paths | accept | Local-only deployment per PROJECT.md; error messages display in app for debugging |
| T-16-08 | DoS | Regex catastrophic backtracking on malicious XML | mitigate | Used non-greedy `[^}]+?` and `[^%]+?` patterns bounded by literal terminators; no nested quantifiers |
</threat_model>

